      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the midpoint of a segment with given endpoints, we use the midpoint formula:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right) \\]\nwhere $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ are the coordinates of the endpoints.\n\nGiven endpoints $(6, 12)$ and $(0, -6)$, we can plug these values into the midpoint formula:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{6 + 0}{2}, \\frac{12 + (-6)}{2} \\right) \\]\nSimplifying the fractions, we get:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{6}{2}, \\frac{6}{2} \\right) \\]\n\\[ \\left( 3, 3 \\right) \\]\n\nThe midpoint of the segment is $(3, 3)$. To find the sum of the coordinates of this midpoint, we simply add the $x$ and $y$ coordinates:\n\\[ 3 + 3 = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coordinates of the midpoint is $\\boxed{6}$.",
